Flow Offload (fastpath) plugin
==============================

Target hardware: PC Engines APU2.

1.04  - Fix "nft list flowtable" syntax so the running fastpath is detected;
        previously the table was reloaded on every job run, appending another
        "flow add @fastpath" rule each time. Rebuild now starts from a clean
        table.

1.03  - Leave the flowtable TCP/UDP inactivity timeouts at the kernel
        default (30 s); they are now an opt-in override in fastpath.conf.
      - Document how to find the NIC's maximum ring-buffer size with
        "ethtool -g" (use the RX/TX values under "Pre-set maximums").

1.02  - Document that this plugin targets PC Engines APU2 hardware.

1.01  - Rebuild the fastpath when its device set (or a device's ifindex)
        changes, eg. when the WAN netdev was removed and brought up again.
        Tracked via a fingerprint stored in /var/tmp/anf_fastpath_state.

1.00  - Initial release.
      - Enable the nftables flowtable fastpath for forwarded TCP/UDP traffic,
        managed in an isolated "inet fastpath" table (never part of the ANF
        "inet anf" batch).
      - Devices default to EXT_IF + INT_IF + DMZ_IF (wildcards expanded),
        overridable with FASTPATH_DEVICES.
      - Optional: raise NIC ring buffers on all hardware NICs (or
        FASTPATH_NIC_RINGS), set the CPU scaling governor, and tune the
        flowtable TCP/UDP timeouts.
      - A background job (re)tries building the fastpath once the WAN
        interface becomes available.
